Package: odumesl
Title: ggplot2 Layers for H.T. Odum's Energy Systems Language
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Eric", "Scheier", email = "hello@emrgi.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides grammar-of-graphics 'ggplot2' layers for the seven
    canonical symbols of H.T. Odum's Energy Systems Language (ESL): source
    circles, producer bullet-nosed hexagons, consumer hexagons, storage
    bullet-tanks, interaction diamonds, heat-sink triangles, and money
    transaction nodes. Each symbol is exposed as a proper 'ggplot2'
    'geom_*' with standard aesthetics ('x', 'y', 'width', 'height',
    'fill', 'colour', 'alpha', 'linewidth'), vectorised over data rows,
    composable in a 'ggplot()' pipeline. Enables ESL diagrams to be
    authored programmatically and quantitatively overlaid on real data
    — including onto the log-transformity spectral hierarchy used in
    Odum's own diagrams. Low-level vertex helpers (returning tibbles
    of polygon coordinates) are also exported for users who want to
    hand-compose 'geom_polygon()' layers. See Brown (2004)
    <doi:10.1016/j.ecolmodel.2003.12.008> for background on ESL
    notation.
